SUMMARY:CARE Seminar: Juan Nicolas Herrera\, University of California\, S
 anta Barbara
LOCATION:North Hall 2111
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Juan Nicolas Herrera\, University of California\, Sa
 nta Barbara\nHosted by: Daniel Martin\n\nJuan Nicolas Herrera earned his
  Bachelor’s in Economics jointly from Universidad del Rosario in Colom
 bia and the Toulouse School of Economics in France. He also holds a Mast
 er’s in Public Policy and Development from the Paris School of Economi
 cs and a Master of Arts in Economics from the University of California\,
  Santa Barbara (UCSB). Prior to joining UCSB\, he was a Research Fellow 
 in the Research Department of the Inter-American Development Bank. Durin
 g his graduate studies\, he served as an instructor for undergraduate co
 urses in public economics and statistics and worked as a research assist
 ant for Professor Alisa Tazhitdinova. His research interests include pub
 lic economics\, housing markets\, labor economics\, and applied economet
 rics. His current research focuses on the incidence of taxation in housi
 ng markets.\n\nhttps://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/care-seminar-juan-n
 icolas-herrera-university-california-santa-barbara
URL:https://econ.ucsb.edu/events/all/2026/care-seminar-juan-nicolas-herre
